# .vercelignore — what the Vercel CLI must never upload as build source.
#
# Why this file exists: Vercel's documented source-upload limit is 100 MB on
# Hobby / 1 GB on Pro (vercel.com/docs/limits). This working tree holds ~409 MB
# of rendered images plus ~81 MB of turntable frames, so a plain `vercel` /
# `vercel --prod` would fail before it ever started a build.
#
# The two media trees are generated artefacts. They are reproduced by the remote
# build itself (vercel.json buildCommand with P911_FETCH_ASSETS=1) or omitted —
# see docs/DEPLOY.md. Nothing here is authored by hand.
#
# NOTE: `.vercelignore` is only consulted by the Vercel CLI. A Git-integrated
# deploy uploads whatever the repository contains, so `public/turntables/**`
# being untracked is a .gitignore concern, not one this file can fix.

# rendered images: everything except the committed silhouette placeholder that
# lib/assets.ts falls back to (and the folder README).
public/images/*
!public/images/_placeholder

# turntable frames (103 sequences)
public/turntables

# build/tooling noise
.cache
node_modules
.next
out
dist
*.log
tsconfig.tsbuildinfo
.DS_Store
.env*.local
.vercel

# research docs are not part of the deployed site
docs